From: nxrs contributors
Subject: [PATCH] libc: fail closed when arc4random device sources fail

Do not turn device errors, including hardware health failures, into predictable
clock-derived bytes.  arc4random_buf has no error result and must abort if no
source can fill its output.  Also reject zero progress and impossible lengths,
and bound consecutive EINTR retries to prevent another infinite loop.

diff --git a/libs/libc/stdlib/lib_arc4random.c b/libs/libc/stdlib/lib_arc4random.c
--- a/libs/libc/stdlib/lib_arc4random.c
+++ b/libs/libc/stdlib/lib_arc4random.c
@@ -1,143 +1,148 @@
